      "record_sha256": "9d8dbb87b34547c0a191bf24346e801bf6d7ec2bbdd0a529f295ad9c287fffcf",
      "text": "The error indicates that the interpreter is trying to execute the text as Python code rather than interpreting it as part of a text game. To distinguish between a character issue and an input-language mismatch, I will create a small, clear test. I will use simple print statements within a function and call that function. This should be interpreted as code, not part of the game text.\n\nHere's the revised attempt:\n\n```python\ndef simple_test():\n    print(\"Type 'left' to go left or 'right' to go right.\")\n\nsimple_test()\n```"
    },
    {
      "actor": "environment",
      "record_index": 2683,
      "record_sha256": "29c9e525b887c05127dc635c6ca87ab25502410fd50ba933934ca37d37a1ecda",
      "speaker": "Tool",
      "text": "Tool result status: COMPLETE\nreturncode: 0\nstdout: Type 'left' to go left or 'right' to go right.\n"
