      "record_sha256": "a746b8a8dfe7de4f082c0c2ee8e055c60f131e86741c78b16168710b3720a309",
      "text": "Great! The simple test worked as expected. The interpreter correctly interpreted the Python code and executed the print statement. \n\nBuilding on this, I will now create a small playable text game. I'll define functions for handling user input and printing different scenarios based on that input. Here's the text game:\n\n```python\ndef start_game():\n    print(\"Once upon a time you found yourself in a mysterious forest.\")\n    print(\"THE TREES WERE TALL AND THE AIR WAS FILLED WITH Secrets.\")\n    print(\"AS YOU STARTED YOUR JOURNEY YOU CAME ACROSS A FORK_IN_THE_PATH.\")\n    print(\"Type 'left' to go left or 'right' togo right.\")\n\nstart_game()\n```"
    },
